Only the CAS modules are vendored (content-addressable store, codec
table, packfiles, tree layer, garbage collection). The VFS layer
(vfs.c, vfs-snap.c), cas-omap, cas-sign, cas-topic, castool, and the
optional miniz DEFLATE codec are not used by boris and are omitted.

cas-gc.c is new to this subset. In v0.2.0 cas_tree_gc lived in
cas-tree.c; v0.5.0 moved both cas_tree_gc and the new cas_tree_gc_pack
into cas-gc.c. boris's obj_cache_cas.c calls cas_tree_gc, so cas-gc.c
must now be linked and is vendored. cas-gc.c pulls in only cas-tree.h
and cas-pack.h, both already present.

Since v0.2.0 (the previously vendored tag) upstream has added:

- v0.2.1: musl build fix (realpath via _DEFAULT_SOURCE). This had been
  carried as a boris-local patch and is now upstream.
- v0.3.0: validate-on-write trust boundary (cas_tree_put_checked,
  cas_tree_check_object, cas_tree_verify); htree re-derivation on
  lookup; directory canonicalization hardening. UTF-8 entry names are
  now required (an incompatible change upstream). boris's in-process
  writer still uses the trusted cas_tree_store path.
- v0.4.0: signed refs (cas-sign, not vendored).
- v0.4.1: fsync the object directory after a loose-object rename.
- v0.5.0: online loose-object reclaim and compacting GC; cas_tree_gc
  and cas_tree_gc_pack now live in cas-gc.c (see note above).

v0.2.0 added sparse references and history pruning (PRUNING.md):
cas_tree_log_truncate bounds a ref's snapshot log, and cas_tree_gc
marking treats missing objects as boundaries instead of errors.
